# match-universal phase 1 — `match` as a universal discriminator (additive)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (additive; every existing match site lowers byte-identically —
# docs/design/plano-match-universal-e-migracao-variant.md §0-§2, §7):
#   - LEFT-OF-ARM RELATION CHECK, in `src/checker/match.tks`. `is_direct_case_of` now takes the type
#     table and, for a NON-variant subject, defers to `is_type_discriminant_of`: a polymorphic
#     BASE-CLASS subject admits a concrete SUBCLASS reaching it (`subclass_reaches`); an INTERFACE
#     subject admits a concrete type conforming to it (`type_conforms_to`); every other subject
#     (struct/primitive/sealed-class/service) admits only itself, the bind-all `type_eq` already
#     accepts — so the change is inert for them. A rejected arm is diagnosed by
#     `discriminant_mismatch_error` ("not a subclass of" / "does not implement", else the historic
#     variant skip-level message).
#   - CLOSED-SET EXHAUSTIVENESS, in `src/checker/match.tks`. `exhaustive`'s non-variant/non-enum tail
#     now routes to `exhaustive_type_subject`: a polymorphic base-class subject is exhaustive iff an
#     unguarded bind-all names the base OR every concrete subclass is covered (`subclasses_of` +
#     `class_covered`); an INTERFACE subject is an OPEN set, exhaustive only via an unguarded
#     catch-all/bind-all; every other subject stays open (false — the pre-existing behavior). A guarded
#     arm (`when`) does NOT count toward covering its case (the existing B.15 rule, reused).
#   - C-BACKEND LOWERING, in `src/codegen/codegen.tks`. A base-class/interface/trait subject is a fat
#     pointer `{ data, vtable }` (W10b.D3 / #98): `cg_fatptr_subject_name` detects it, and
#     `cg_emit_fatptr_pat_test`/`cg_emit_fatptr_pat_binds` discriminate an arm by comparing the
#     subject's `.vtable` word against that concrete's `tk_vt_<Concrete>_<Subject>` array and bind the
#     concrete off `.data`. A bind-all naming the subject matches unconditionally and binds the whole
#     value. The native backend carries no per-object vtable, so its fat-pointer dispatch stays the
#     existing N2 honest-stop (unchanged this phase).
# WHAT DOES NOT ENTER: no `variant` type is migrated; literal/range patterns on the left still parse
# and work (Phase 2); no `properties`/interface get-set.
#
# INERTNESS. A real-build scan of the compiler's own emitted C shows the ONLY new `teko_teko__`
# symbols are the phase-1 additions (`checker::{is_type_discriminant_of, discriminant_mismatch_error,
# subclasses_of, class_covered, exhaustive_type_subject}`, `codegen::{cg_fatptr_subject_name,
# cg_emit_fatptr_pat_test, cg_emit_fatptr_pat_binds}`) plus `checker::subclass_reaches` (an existing
# function now reachable as a standalone symbol) — ZERO removed symbols, so no existing match site is
# lowered differently. The whole 153-file compiler re-checks and self-builds green.
#
